invariant: INV-48
file: src/mlkem_avx2.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh mlkem-avx2
reason: a step of the rejection step on AVX2 runs while eight more
  coefficients fit, not sixteen, so from a count of 241 to 248 it keeps
  up to 16 candidates, writes past coefficient 255 and returns a count
  above 256. bin/mlkem_avx2_equiv_test starts the step at 247, 248 and
  249 and requires mlk_sample_groups's count. Only an x86-64 compiler
  reads the line, so the script builds the test for x86-64 and runs it
  under qemu-x86_64. The lane skips without docker, and this then reports
  unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    for (; group + 8 <= groups && j <= MLKEM_N - 16; group += 8) {
--- new
    for (; group + 8 <= groups && j <= MLKEM_N - 8; group += 8) {
